{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01YZo1vjXWbFPfc94WxBCLQn","input":{"content":"---\nname: local-model-oneshot-evaluation\ndescription: \"User has the local DeepSeek model one-shot substantial features, then asks Claude to review — the review IS the capability measurement\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nevintunador uses turnbridge features as a capability benchmark for the local\nDeepSeek V4 Flash model (ds4-gateway): he asks it to one-shot a substantial\ntask, opens a PR without smoke-testing it, and then asks Claude to review.\nObserved 2026-08-03 on PR #3 (opencode target adapter): \"I'm looking to get an\nidea of whether that complexity of task is doable for an open model.\"\n\n**Why:** the review's real purpose is two-sided — fix the PR *and* characterize\nwhere the open model's output breaks down. A verdict of \"looks fine\" without\nexecution is worthless to him; the interesting signal is which specific class\nof thing the model got right versus wrong. On PR #3 the pattern was: format\nreverse-engineering from a real export was largely correct, but every defect\ncame from validating only the happy path (tool-call payloads failed import\noutright, and there were no tests at all).\n\n**How to apply:** when reviewing local-model work, actually execute it against\nthe real CLI rather than reading it — the defects live in the branches the\nmodel could not observe. Report the failure *pattern*, not just a defect list.\nRelated: [[evintunador-workflow-preferences]], [[turnbridge-mvp-decisions]].\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/memory/local-model-oneshot-evaluation.md"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"fix/opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/opencode-fixes","dirty_fingerprint":"cf8b9e3c1e47cd671f179e23127d98edb70689fbf4ed08f9960baec974f11cfc","head":"7bf348e083a26b95afb6